Incident-01-Phishing Attack
Inbound Email Containing Suspicious External Link

Overview:
An alert was generated indicating an inbound email containing a suspicious external URL. 
The alert required investigation to determine whether malicious activity was present and whether escalation was necessary.

Analyst information:
Analyst Role: SOC Level 1 Analyst (Simulation)
Investigation Environment: TryHackMe Lab Environment
Alert Severity: Medium
Time to Resolve: 6.67 minutes
Investigation Date: 13 May 2026


Alert details:
Alert Name: Inbound Email Containing Suspicious External Link
Timestamp: 05/13/2026 20:45:08.833
Affected User: h.harris@thetrydaily.thm
The alert indicated potential phishing activity due to the presence of an external URL embedded within the email body.

Investigation process:
Reviewd all infomation and metadata provided for the alert, Confirmed alert originated from email security monitoring system.

URL analysis:
Examined the URL contained in the email body, Security analysis tools within the virtual machine environment identified the URL as malicious.

Threat Validation:
Verified malicious classification using investigation tools.
Determined the email represented a phishing attempt designed to redirect the recipient to a harmful external resource.

Findings:
Email contained a confirmed malicious external link.
High likelihood of credential harvesting or malware delivery.
No evidence provided of successful compromise at investigation time.

Alert classification: true positive


Indicators of comrpomise:
suspicious inbound email, external fishing URL

MITRE ATT&CH mapping:
Initial Access — Phishing (T1566)

Potential risks included:
1. malware delivery
2. credential comrpomise
3. unathorized account login


Escalation decision:
the attack was escalated because it contained malicious URL and user interaction could lead to account compromise.

Recommended remediation actions:
1. notify affected user
2. remove or quarantine malicious email
3. reset user credential if interaction occured
4. monitor account activity for suspicious behaviour
5. spread phishing awareness


Lessons learned:
This investigation demonstrates the importance of rapid phishing triage and 
validation of external links to prevent credential compromise within enterprise environments.


Skills demonstrated:
Security alert triage
Phishing investigation
Threat validation
SOC escalation procedures
Incident documentation
Analyst decision-making
